<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Flensburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Flensburg is a port city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, at the head of the Flensburg Fjord close to the Danish border. Part of the Danish realm for centuries, it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1864 and remained German after the plebiscite of 1920. In May 1945 it was the seat of the last government of Nazi Germany under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-donitz">Karl Dönitz</a>, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> arrested on 23 May.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/flensburg.jpg" alt="Flensburg" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wolfgang Pehlemann · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luftbild_Flensburg_Schleswig-Holstein_Zentrum_Stadthafen_Foto_2012_Wolfgang_Pehlemann_Steinberg-Ostsee_IMG_6187.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
